On Friday 21 November 2003 15:48 Zwanth wrote:

> - If you find an altar, you can drop things on it to find out if
> they're blessed, uncursed, or cursed.  You can also #offer fresh
> monster corpses on it.

Take care (while you're still a newbie) that you sacrifice on an altar
to your own god, especially if you're low level. Once you're
comfortable with altars and alignment, you can graduate to converting
cross-aligned (= not to your own god) altars.

Oh, and don't sacrifice your deceased pet (you can safely eat it if it
isn't a cat or a dog, or you're a cave(wo)man), and don't sacrifice
your own species unless you're chaotic.

> - If you find a wand, you can engrave with it and it might give you a
> clue as to what it does.  e.g. if you get "The bugs on the floor slow
> down!" then it's a wand of slow monster.

It's wise to scribble something in the dust with your fingers first;
there are some wands that do something with the message that's already
there and don't have any effect when there's no previous writing.
(polymorph makes it something else, cancellation and make invisible
make it disappear, teleportation moves it to elsewhere on the level -
in effect it also disappears).

